//:: cases TC_CB_6_AssertFalseGap
//:: tools silicon
//:: verdict Fail

// TC-CB-6: Documented gap — assert false is different from assume false.
// assert false is a proof obligation: it fails with assertFailed, but does NOT
// add false to the state. The verifier does not treat subsequent code as dead.
//
// Verdict is Fail due to assertFailed on the assert itself, NOT due to
// refute false firing. The branch after assert false is still considered live.
void f(int x) {
    assert false; // assertFailed: state is feasible, so false never holds
    if (x > 0) {
        x = x + 1; // NOT dead: assert false does not narrow the state
    }
}
